#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064099 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064117 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022d7b7b-070a-51f5-bd49-94b4db34c49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247437} {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} {:answer/id #uuid "76108c8b-8f42-5f4a-9dd2-e847f09e6e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248463} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfdc77f-bbbe-57f4-9329-f07738aa11a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248678} {:answer/id #uuid "c6440ae3-1132-5195-b3a2-356c7752e48e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} :answer-field/id #uuid "eede1f3b-85f2-5008-b473-3fcd59ae080b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "872e80da-db87-5cbe-89ef-83c58a2b3950" :question/math-academy-id "q-114289" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{3}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & ={3}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{3}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248350} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248682} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} {:answer/id #uuid "394ffebc-fc15-59d2-b922-cf67e8668a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257288} {:answer/id #uuid "98f26b34-1c20-50e4-ae9f-0696b345d0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258130} {:answer/id #uuid "dee11791-9fa1-5f13-86b4-6751c7ac156e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258723} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7bf65f-10a0-5fb7-85b0-318f615112d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} :answer-field/id #uuid "4626c1aa-c3c9-5543-a9d9-8d0984251445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d57f8c60-94ea-5515-8561-35af7ac97700" :question/math-academy-id "q-12556" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043fa24a-45ec-5b10-bfa8-7e31faa50866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272422} {:answer/id #uuid "4dad317a-7e2c-5027-9a3a-188de187c660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273038} {:answer/id #uuid "657c9906-4184-54b2-a2ca-75931266448c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273256} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6fa9bf-7209-5009-8683-0533f03518a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274192} {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b869c77-052f-508f-90ff-9807f6d71398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36f423a0-7a02-5e68-b537-f427610136e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14437" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398c3cee-657c-5b95-8a1e-1aa70b615cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330468} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6624a0-3597-520a-b136-40dc699a2c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330632} {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} {:answer/id #uuid "b6aee3a4-6d54-578c-8449-e0741c41a98f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331563} {:answer/id #uuid "cea8bab6-1bfc-5d6a-a36b-eda9ee31a503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a32b33d9-9824-5fca-9f78-08bd81319767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d08b82b1-573b-56aa-9196-6973e5625acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-49664" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)]+[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0]+[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
